# uv.lock and .python-version ARE committed (reproducibility, same reasoning as
# package-lock.json) - not listed here on purpose

# AI tooling. Machine-local state stays untracked; workflow *definitions* are
# tracked, because .specify/memory/constitution.md cites them by path as
# authoritative and Principle III mandates the commands they implement - a repo
# that references them without shipping them is referencing files that do not
# exist. See docs/DECISIONS.md.
#
# Tracked:   .claude/skills/, .specify/memory/constitution.md, .specify/templates/
# Untracked: editor/machine settings, worktrees, CLAUDE.md (its content is already
#            covered by constitution.md and docs/DESIGN.md), and per-feature
#            tasks.md / checklists (internal implementation checklists by design).
.claude/*
!.claude/skills
CLAUDE.md
.specify/*
!.specify/memory
!.specify/templates
.specify/memory/*
!.specify/memory/constitution.md
specs/*/tasks.md
specs/*/checklists/

# Interview-corpus raw cache and working state — large and/or re-derivable from
# sources.yaml + the fetcher scripts, not source of truth. Tracked instead:
# corpus/sources.yaml, corpus/_meta/manifest/, corpus/_meta/candidates/,
# corpus/licenses/, corpus/summary.json, corpus/reports/.
#
# candidates/ is tracked because it is NOT re-derivable: each row is a concept a human
# accepted into the corpus (hard constraint 7), and concept_id may never be renamed once
# admitted. Regenerating it means redoing the review, not rerunning a script.
corpus/raw/
corpus/.venv/
corpus/_meta/*
!corpus/_meta/manifest/
!corpus/_meta/candidates/
